<form class="form-horizontal">
  <div class="alert">
    Every value here ends up in a G-code command. The plugin checks each value when you
    save and again before each run. It refuses a point outside the plate.
  </div>

  <h4>Heat and brush</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Bed, &deg;C</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.bed_temp">
      <span class="help-block">
        The plate is measured at this temperature, so use the one you print at. The bed
        stays hot for the whole run.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">T0 and T1, &deg;C</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.t0_temp">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.t1_temp">
      <span class="help-block">
        Hot enough to soften the filament in each nozzle, so the brush can remove it.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Retract, mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.retract_mm">
      <span class="help-block">
        Pulls the filament back so the hot nozzles do not ooze while you brush them. The
        next print primes it again.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Park X, Y, Z</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-medium"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.park">
      <span class="help-block">Where the head waits while you brush the nozzles.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Brush time limit, min</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.wipe_timeout_min">
      <span class="help-block">
        If nobody presses Continue in this time, the heaters go off and the run stops.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Cool</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Touch below, &deg;C</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.cool_below">
      <span class="help-block">
        The nozzles touch the plate only when both are below this. Soft plastic on a
        warm tip squashes and reads high.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Settle, s</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="10" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.settle_s">
      <span class="help-block">A wait after the fans stop, so the plate stops moving.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Touch</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Passes</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.passes">
      <span class="help-block">
        Each pass touches all 100 reachable nodes and takes about 25 min. The mesh is
        the mean of the passes. One pass is good to about 0.03 mm, two to about 0.02 mm.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Reference X, Y</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-medium"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.reference">
      <span class="help-block">
        Touched before each row. While the machine sits hot the trip height drifts by
        up to 0.2 mm an hour, and this point measures the drift so it can be removed.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Sensor travel, mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.01" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.trip_to_zero">
      <span class="help-block">
        How far the carriage moves after the nozzle first touches the plate, before its
        sensor trips. The mesh adds it back, so G-code Z 0 sits on the plate. 0.72 mm
        was measured with a clean nozzle on 2026-09-25. Change it only after a first
        layer test says to.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>T1 height</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Points</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xxlarge"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.offset_points">
      <span class="help-block">
        X, Y pairs with a semicolon between them. Both nozzles touch each point. The
        new offset makes both nozzles trip at the same height on average.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.write_offset">
        Write the new T1 offset with M218. The toolhead stores it at once.
      </label>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>After the run</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.bed_off_at_end">
        Turn the bed off at the end.
      </label>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Serial</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.nozzletouch.fix_split_ok">
        Restore a lost acknowledgement at all times, not only during a run.
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">
        When a nozzle is pushed up, the toolhead sends "active extruder mismatch" at once.
        When that message lands inside the firmware's "ok", OctoPrint loses the ok and
        stops sending. The plugin sees the damaged line and gives OctoPrint the ok back.
        During a run this is always on.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</form>
